**File:** `src/components/log/TrainingLogCard.tsx`

Both `logNeedsImprovement` and `getWeakLogReasons` are called per card render, but `logNeedsImprovement` just calls `getWeakLogReasons` internally — so `getWeakLogReasons` runs twice per log:

```tsx
// Current — double computation
const weakLog = logNeedsImprovement(log);   // calls getWeakLogReasons internally
const weakReasons = getWeakLogReasons(log); // called again

// Fix — compute once
const weakReasons = getWeakLogReasons(log);
const weakLog = weakReasons.length > 0;
```

---

**File:** `src/utils/reportBuilder.ts`

`buildWeeklyReport` iterates `logs` at least 4 separate times (sort+slice, two filters, plus all the utility calls that also iterate internally). The two explicit filters can be combined:

```ts
// Current
const weakLogs = logs.filter((log) => getWeakLogReasons(log).length > 0);
const fatigueWatchLogs = logs.filter((log) => isFatigueWatch(log.readiness));

// Fix — single pass
let weakCount = 0;
let fatigueCount = 0;
for (const log of logs) {
  if (getWeakLogReasons(log).length > 0) weakCount++;
  if (isFatigueWatch(log.readiness)) fatigueCount++;
}
```

This matters since `getWeakLogReasons` is non-trivial (regex, multiple checks) and runs on every log.

---

**File:** `src/screens/LogScreen.tsx`

`handleRecommendationAction`, `clearSearchAndFilters`, and `confirmDeleteLog` are recreated on every render. They're passed as props to child components, causing unnecessary child re-renders:

```tsx
// Fix
const handleRecommendationAction = useCallback((actionType: RecommendationActionType) => {
  if (actionType === 'weak-logs') setShowWeakLogsOnly(true);
  else router.push('/add-log');
}, [router]);

const clearSearchAndFilters = useCallback(() => {
  setActiveFilter('All');
  setSortMode('Newest');
  setSearchQuery('');
  setShowWeakLogsOnly(false);
}, []);

const confirmDeleteLog = useCallback((log: TrainingLog) => {
  // ...
}, [deleteLog]);
```

---

**File:** `src/screens/LogScreen.tsx` + `src/components/log/TrainingLogCard.tsx`

`getWeakLogReasons` runs per `TrainingLogCard` render. Since `logs` is the stable input, compute weak reasons once in `LogScreen` and pass them down:

```tsx
// In LogScreen
const weakReasonsMap = useMemo(() => {
  const map = new Map<number, string[]>();
  for (const log of logs) {
    const reasons = getWeakLogReasons(log);
    if (reasons.length > 0) map.set(log.id, reasons);
  }
  return map;
}, [logs]);

// Pass to TrainingLogCard
<TrainingLogCard
  log={item}
  weakReasons={weakReasonsMap.get(item.id) ?? []}
  onEdit={...}
  onDelete={...}
/>
```

This avoids re-running validation logic on every render of every visible card.

---

**File:** `src/components/log/TrainingLogForm.tsx`

`getQuickTemplates()` is called inside the component and creates `new Date()` on every render:

```tsx
// Current — called inline, re-runs on every render
const quickTemplates = getQuickTemplates();

// Fix — memoize or move to module-level with stable date handling
// Since date is "today", useMemo with no deps (or a daily key) is sufficient
const quickTemplates = useMemo(() => getQuickTemplates(), []);
```

---

**File:** `src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx`

`getStrengthStatus`, `getEnduranceStatus`, and `getRecoveryStatus` each filter `logs` independently, plus `logs.find` is called 4 more times — that's 7 separate iterations over the same array:

```tsx
// Fix — single pass to derive all derived data
const derived = useMemo(() => {
  const strengthLogs: TrainingLog[] = [];
  const enduranceLogs: TrainingLog[] = [];
  let latestRuck: TrainingLog | undefined;
  let latestStrength: TrainingLog | undefined;
  let latestRun: TrainingLog | undefined;
  let latestRecovery: TrainingLog | undefined;
  let recentFatigue = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < logs.length; i++) {
    const l = logs[i];
    if (l.category === 'Strength') strengthLogs.push(l);
    if (l.category === 'Ruck' || l.category === 'Run') enduranceLogs.push(l);
    if (!latestRuck && l.category === 'Ruck') latestRuck = l;
    if (!latestStrength && l.category === 'Strength') latestStrength = l;
    if (!latestRun && l.category === 'Run') latestRun = l;
    if (!latestRecovery && l.category === 'Recovery') latestRecovery = l;
    if (i < 5 && getReadinessNumber(l.readiness) <= 5) recentFatigue++;
  }
  return { strengthLogs, enduranceLogs, latestRuck, latestStrength, latestRun, latestRecovery, recentFatigue };
}, [logs]);
```

